  "summary": {
    "ideas": [
      "A recurrence relation $u_{n+1} = f(u_n)$ builds each term from the one before, from a starting term.",
      "If the terms settle at $L$, the sequence **converges** to $L$, and $L = f(L)$: solve it to find $L$.",
      "Terms settle only when each step shrinks the gap to $L$; otherwise they run away."
    ],
    "formula": {
      "name": "Where a recurrence settles",
      "tex": "u_{n+1} = au_n + b \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad L = \\dfrac{b}{1 - a}",
      "note": "The terms move towards $L$ only when $-1 < a < 1$."
    },
    "trap": "The rule feeds in the last term $u_n$, never the position $n$."
  },
